-- title:
--   Chart addition law for a pinned addition morphism off the diagonal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, and $F$ a field that is an $R$-algebra such that the image of the discriminant $W.\Delta$ under $R \to F$ is nonzero. Write $E = \mathrm{Proj}$ of the graded ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,3, R)$ modulo the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of `W.toProjective`, with its structure morphism `projModelStrCR` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$, and for $i : \mathrm{Fin}\,3$ let $\mathcal{A}_i$ be the degree-zero homogeneous localisation of that graded quotient away from the class of $X_i$, an $R$-algebra via the degree-zero part. Let $m : E \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,R} E \to E$ be a morphism subject to the pinning hypothesis `hmpin`: for all $i, j : \mathrm{Fin}\,3$ and all $l : \mathrm{Fin}\,3 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,3$, the composite of the localisation map $\mathrm{Spec}\,(\mathrm{Localization.Away}\,(\mathtt{kw\_lrSixU}\,W\,i\,j\,l)) \to \mathrm{Spec}((\mathcal{A}_i) \otimes_R (\mathcal{A}_j))$ with the inverse of the isomorphism identifying the $(i,j)$ chart of the pullback with $\mathrm{Spec}((\mathcal{A}_i) \otimes_R (\mathcal{A}_j))$, the inclusion of that chart into the pullback, and $m$, equals `kw_lrSixU_toE W i j l`, that is, $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the ring map `kw_lrChart_tensor W i j k` (respectively `kw_lrSymChart_tensor W i j k`, according to the summand of $l$) followed by the open immersion `Proj.awayι` of the $k$-th chart of $E$. Let $i, j, k : \mathrm{Fin}\,3$ and let $\psi_i : \mathcal{A}_i \to F$, $\psi_j : \mathcal{A}_j \to F$, $\psi_k : \mathcal{A}_k \to F$ be $R$-algebra maps. Let $x$ and $y$ be $F$-points of $E$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$, i.e. morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}\,F \to E$ whose composite with the structure morphism is $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $R \to F$, and assume $x$ factors as $\mathrm{Spec}\,\psi_i$ followed by the $i$-th chart inclusion of the affine open cover of $E$, and $y$ as $\mathrm{Spec}\,\psi_j$ followed by the $j$-th chart inclusion. Assume further that the induced morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,F \to E \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,R} E$ determined by $x$ and $y$, followed by $m$, equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\psi_k$ followed by the $k$-th chart inclusion, and that the two projective point classes $\llbracket (\psi_i(\mathrm{gen}\,i\,0), \psi_i(\mathrm{gen}\,i\,1), \psi_i(\mathrm{gen}\,i\,2)) \rrbracket$ and $\llbracket (\psi_j(\mathrm{gen}\,j\,\bullet)) \rrbracket$ in $\mathrm{WeierstrassCurve.Projective.PointClass}\,F$ are distinct. The conclusion is that the class of the coordinate triple $(\psi_k(\mathrm{gen}\,k\,\bullet))$ equals the value of `addMap` for the projective Weierstrass curve $(W \otimes_R F).\mathrm{toProjective}$ on the classes coming from $\psi_i$ and $\psi_j$.
--
--   This identifies, on $F$-points lying off the diagonal, an arbitrary morphism $E \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,R} E \to E$ that is pinned to the explicit Lange–Ruppert addition formulae on the six distinguished opens of each tensor chart with the classical projective group law `addMap` of the base-changed Weierstrass curve. It is the input to the density arguments used to verify the group-law axioms for such a pinned morphism, among them `pin_addMorphism_assoc` and the existence statements for point evaluations.
